+# Broadcom research provenance
+
+Consulted on 2026-08-15. The installer plan uses the exercise's pinned snapshot when a live page is newer or less specific.
+
+| Broadcom publication | Reachable URL | Architectural fact used |
+|---|---|---|
+| Upgrade of Aria Operations 8.18.6 or 8.18.7 to VCF Operations 9.0.x is Unsupported | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/438994 | A direct 8.18.6-to-9.0.x upgrade is explicitly unsupported. The supported alternative is a greenfield VCF Operations 9.0.2 deployment with export/import of dashboards, super metrics, views, and reports; historical time-series metrics do not migrate. |
+| Import and upgrade VMware Aria Automation 8.x to VCF Automation 9.0 | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/433806 | The inventoried 8.18.0 legacy Lifecycle-managed Automation instance is imported as an integrated instance into VCF Operations Fleet Management before its VCF Automation 9.0 upgrade is triggered. |
+| Users unable to view their existing deployments after upgrading from Aria Automation 8.18 to VCF Automation 9.0.x | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/434594 | Existing deployments remain after upgrade, but identity principals are normalized to lowercase; the cutover therefore needs an identity-case validation gate. |
+| Upgrade Guidance for Aria Operations for Logs 8.18.x to VCF Operations for Logs 9.0.x | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/402314 | The inventoried Logs 8.18.2 has no in-place 9.0.x upgrade. A fresh target runs in parallel, integrations are removed and recreated, and at most 90 days of log data can be transferred. |
+| Getting started with VMware Cloud Foundation or VMware vSphere Foundation V9 Licensing | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/437242 | Version 9 licensing is administered by VCF Operations. One license allocation cannot be used by two VCF Operations instances, and vCenter assignment licenses downstream VCF components. This makes the fixture's unsplittable single allocation incompatible with per-site fleets. |
+| VCF Operations 9.0 Sizing Guidelines | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/397782 | The 9.0 guidance defines Operations node and cloud-proxy profiles and lists the 16-vCPU/32-GB large Logs profile; production Logs clusters have a three-node minimum. These facts support the selected profiles while the pinned snapshot fixes disk and appliance-specific values. |
+| End of General Support for VMware Aria Operations 8.18 | https://knowledge.broadcom.com/external/article/422643 | The live notice places Aria Operations 8.18 end of general support on 2027-10-11, after the estate's required 2027-06-30 completion date. The pinned snapshot supplies the deterministic boundary used for all three source mappings. |
